BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the switch-case statement, explaining integral expression constraints, fall-through mechanics, and jump tables.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The switch-case Statement and Jump-Table Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   1. Syntactical Structure and Constraints:) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluates an expression against multiple discrete constant values.) Tj
T*
(   - Expression Constraint: MUST evaluate to an integer type \(char, short, int, long, enum\).) Tj
T*
(   Floating-point \(float/double\) and strings are strictly prohibited!) Tj
T*
(   - Case Label Constraint: Must be a compile-time constant expression. Variables \(case x:\) are) Tj
T*
(   illegal.) Tj
T*
(   - Duplicate Labels: Two case labels cannot have identical values in the same switch scope.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Fall-Through Execution:) Tj
T*
(   - When a matching case label is reached, execution begins and continues through all subsequent) Tj
T*
(   cases until a 'break' statement or the closing brace is reached.) Tj
T*
(   - Intentional Fall-Through: Used to group multiple cases requiring identical handling:) Tj
T*
(   case 'a':) Tj
T*
(   case 'A':) Tj
T*
(   handle_adenine\(\);) Tj
T*
(   break;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Compiler Optimization: Jump Tables \(Branch Tables\):) Tj
T*
(   - When case values are densely clustered \(e.g. 1, 2, 3, 4, 5\), optimizing compilers do not) Tj
T*
(   generate a slow chain of sequential comparisons \(like an else-if ladder\).) Tj
T*
(   - Instead, the compiler generates a Jump Table \(array of code addresses\).) Tj
T*
(   - The expression serves as an index directly into the jump table: execution jumps to the target) Tj
T*
(   address in constant time O\(1\), regardless of the number of cases!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Demonstrative ANSI C Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   void process_nucleotide\(char base\) {) Tj
T*
(   switch \(base\) {) Tj
T*
(   case 'A': case 'a':) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Adenine \(Purine\): Pairs with Thymine \(2 H-bonds\)\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(   break;) Tj
T*
(   case 'G': case 'g':) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Guanine \(Purine\): Pairs with Cytosine \(3 H-bonds\)\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(   break;) Tj
T*
(   case 'C': case 'c':) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Cytosine \(Pyrimidine\): Pairs with Guanine \(3 H-bonds\)\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(   break;) Tj
T*
(   case 'T': case 't':) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Thymine \(Pyrimidine\): Pairs with Adenine \(2 H-bonds\)\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(   break;) Tj
T*
(   case 'U': case 'u':) Tj
T*
ET

