(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Compare while, do-while, and for loops in C, contrasting entry-controlled vs exit-controlled evaluation with practical use-cases.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Loop Structures in C: while vs do-while vs for:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operational Classification:) Tj
T*
(   - Entry-Controlled Loops \(while, for\):) Tj
T*
(   The loop continuation condition is tested BEFORE executing the loop body. If the condition is) Tj
T*
(   false initially, the loop body executes ZERO times.) Tj
T*
(   - Exit-Controlled Loops \(do-while\):) Tj
T*
(   The condition is tested AFTER executing the loop body. The body is GUARANTEED to execute AT) Tj
T*
(   LEAST ONCE, regardless of initial condition state.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comparative Matrix:) Tj
T*
(   Feature while Loop do-while Loop for Loop) Tj
T*
(   Test Position Entry \(Top\) Exit \(Bottom\) Entry \(Top\)) Tj
T*
(   Minimum Executions 0 1 0) Tj
T*
(   Trailing Semicolon No YES: while\(cond\); No) Tj
T*
(   Best Used For Unknown iterations, User menu prompts, Known iteration count,) Tj
T*
(   sentinel streaming validation loops array indexing) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Syntactical Structures:) Tj
T*
(   - while \(condition\) { statements; }) Tj
T*
(   - do { statements; } while \(condition\);) Tj
T*
(   - for \(init; condition; update\) { statements; }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Equivalence Between for and while:) Tj
T*
(   The for loop:) Tj
T*
(   for \(init_expr; test_expr; update_expr\) { body; }) Tj
T*
(   is semantically identical to:) Tj
T*
(   init_expr;) Tj
T*
(   while \(test_expr\) {) Tj
T*
(   body;) Tj
T*
(   update_expr;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   \(Exception: A 'continue' statement in while skips update_expr, whereas in for it executes) Tj
T*
(   update_expr before the next test\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
