(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Jump Statements in C \(break, continue, goto, return\), detailing execution semantics and structured programming principles.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Jump Statements in C: break, continue, goto, and return:) Tj
T*
(   Jump statements perform unconditional branching, immediately redirecting program control to) Tj
T*
(   another point.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. The break Statement:) Tj
T*
(   - Terminates execution of the immediate innermost enclosing loop \(for, while, do-while\) or) Tj
T*
(   switch statement.) Tj
