(   [Problem Statement]: Write a complete ANSI C program to test whether a given positive integer is prime using optimized trial division up to sqrt\(N\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Optimized Prime Number Testing Program:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Rationale:) Tj
T*
(   - A prime number is an integer greater than 1 with no positive divisors other than 1 and) Tj
T*
(   itself.) Tj
T*
(   - Optimization: If integer N is composite, it can be factored as N = a * b. If both a and b) Tj
T*
(   were strictly greater than sqrt\(N\), their product would exceed N. Hence, at least one factor) Tj
T*
(   must be <= sqrt\(N\).) Tj
T*
(   - Even Number Elimination: Check divisibility by 2. If N is even and > 2, it is composite. All) Tj
T*
(   subsequent trial divisors can skip even numbers \(step by 2: 3, 5, 7, 9, ...\).) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(sqrt\(N\)\) versus O\(N\) brute force.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

