(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to compute the Greatest Common Divisor \(GCD\) using the Euclidean Algorithm and find the LCM.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Euclidean Algorithm for GCD and LCM Computation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Foundation:) Tj
T*
(   - Theorem: For any two non-negative integers a and b \(where a >= b\):) Tj
T*
(   GCD\(a, b\) = GCD\(b, a % b\)) Tj
T*
(   Base case: GCD\(a, 0\) = a.) Tj
T*
(   - LCM Identity: The product of two numbers equals the product of their GCD and LCM:) Tj
T*
(   LCM\(a, b\) = \(a * b\) / GCD\(a, b\)) Tj
T*
(   To avoid integer overflow in \(a * b\), divide first: LCM = \(a / GCD\(a, b\)\) * b.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   long long compute_gcd\(long long a, long long b\) {) Tj
T*
(   while \(b != 0\) {) Tj
T*
(   long long remainder = a % b;) Tj
T*
(   a = b;) Tj
T*
(   b = remainder;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   return a;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
ET

