(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to verify whether a given positive integer is an Armstrong Number \(Narcissistic Number\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Armstrong Number \(Narcissistic Number\) Verification:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition:) Tj
T*
(   An n-digit number is an Armstrong number if the sum of its digits, each raised to the n-th) Tj
T*
(   power, equals the number itself:) Tj
T*
(   For 3 digits: 153 = 1^3 + 5^3 + 3^3 = 1 + 125 + 27 = 153.) Tj
T*
(   For 371: 3^3 + 7^3 + 1^3 = 27 + 343 + 1 = 371.) Tj
T*
(   For 4 digits: 1634 = 1^4 + 6^4 + 3^4 + 4^4 = 1 + 1296 + 81 + 256 = 1634.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Algorithmic Steps:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Count total number of digits \(n\) by repeatedly dividing by 10.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Traverse digits again, computing digit^n using an accumulator.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Compare sum with original value.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete ANSI C Source Code:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdbool.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   long long integer_power\(int base, int exp\) {) Tj
T*
(   long long result = 1;) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < exp; i++\) {) Tj
T*
(   result *= base;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   return result;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   bool is_armstrong\(int num\) {) Tj
T*
(   if \(num < 0\) return false;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* 1. Count number of digits */) Tj
T*
(   int temp = num;) Tj
T*
(   int digits = 0;) Tj
T*
(   while \(temp > 0\) {) Tj
T*
(   digits++;) Tj
T*
(   temp /= 10;) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
