(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to compute the roots of a quadratic equation ax^2 + bx + c = 0, handling real, equal, and complex roots.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Quadratic Equation Solver with Complex Root Support:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mathematical Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   Equation: a * x^2 + b * x + c = 0, where a != 0.) Tj
T*
(   Discriminant \(D\) = b^2 - 4 * a * c:) Tj
T*
(   - Case 1 \(D > 0\): Two distinct real roots: x1, x2 = \(-b +/- sqrt\(D\)\) / \(2a\).) Tj
T*
(   - Case 2 \(D == 0\): Two equal real roots: x1 = x2 = -b / \(2a\).) Tj
T*
(   - Case 3 \(D < 0\): Two conjugate complex roots: Real part = -b / \(2a\), Imaginary part = +/-) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\(-D\) / \(2a\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
