(   [Problem Statement]: Write an ANSI C program to calculate the sum of digits of a positive integer until a single digit root is obtained \(digital root\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Digital Root \(Repeated Sum of Digits\) in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Algorithmic Logic:) Tj
T*
(   Given positive integer N, iteratively sum its decimal digits. If the resulting sum has two or) Tj
T*
(   more digits, repeat the process until a single digit \(0-9\) remains.) Tj
T*
(   Example: 9875 -> 9+8+7+5 = 29 -> 2+9 = 11 -> 1+1 = 2. Digital root = 2.) Tj
T*
(   Number Theory Shortcut: The digital root is congruent to N modulo 9:) Tj
T*
(   Digital Root = 1 + \(\(N - 1\) % 9\) for N > 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Complete ANSI C Source Code \(Iterative & Modular\):) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int compute_digital_root_iterative\(int n\) {) Tj
T*
(   while \(n >= 10\) {) Tj
T*
(   int sum = 0;) Tj
T*
(   while \(n > 0\) {) Tj
T*
(   sum += \(n % 10\);) Tj
T*
