(   2. Loop Unrolling Rationale:) Tj
T*
(   Standard byte copying:) Tj
T*
(   do { *to = *from++; } while \(--count > 0\);) Tj
T*
(   Every single byte copied incurs branch instruction overhead and loop condition decrementing.) Tj
T*
(   Unrolling the loop 8 times reduces loop branch overhead by 87.5%!) Tj
T*
(   Challenge: What if the total count is not an exact multiple of 8?) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Revolutionary Syntactical Insight:) Tj
T*
(   In ANSI C, case labels inside a switch block are legal anywhere inside enclosed compound) Tj
T*
(   statements, EVEN INSIDE A WHILE LOOP!) Tj
T*
(   Tom Duff nested a do-while loop directly across switch case labels!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Annotated Code Listing:) Tj
T*
(   void send_data\(register short *to, register short *from, register int count\) {) Tj
T*
(   register int n = \(count + 7\) / 8;) Tj
T*
(   switch \(count % 8\) {) Tj
T*
(   case 0: do { *to = *from++;) Tj
T*
(   case 7: *to = *from++;) Tj
T*
(   case 6: *to = *from++;) Tj
T*
(   case 5: *to = *from++;) Tj
T*
(   case 4: *to = *from++;) Tj
T*
(   case 3: *to = *from++;) Tj
T*
(   case 2: *to = *from++;) Tj
T*
(   case 1: *to = *from++;) Tj
T*
(   } while \(--n > 0\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Execution Flow:) Tj
T*
(   - switch \(count % 8\) calculates remainder \(0-7\) and jumps directly to the appropriate case) Tj
T*
(   label to copy initial leftover elements.) Tj
T*
(   - Execution falls through to case 1, where the while \(--n > 0\) is encountered.) Tj
T*
(   - If n > 0, the loop wraps back to the 'do' before case 0, subsequently executing all 8 copy) Tj
T*
(   operations in full rounds!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
