T*
(   In-Place Array Reversal Using Pointers and while Loop:) Tj
T*
(   1. Two-Pointer In-Place Technique:) Tj
T*
(   - Establish two pointer variables: 'left' pointing to the first element \(arr[0]\), and 'right') Tj
T*
(   pointing to the last element \(arr[n - 1]\).) Tj
T*
(   - Execute while \(left < right\):) Tj
T*
(   Swap values pointed to by left and right using a temporary scalar variable.) Tj
T*
(   Increment left \(left++ advances pointer forward by sizeof\(int\)\).) Tj
T*
(   Decrement right \(right-- retreats pointer backward\).) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(1\) auxiliary space \(no secondary array allocated\).) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(N\) comparisons and N/2 swaps.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
